WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.550
When did you last look at your policies?

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:04.810
Life changes:

3
00:00:04.997 --> 00:00:09.675
a marriage, a child, a new loan, a new job.

4
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:13.401
Policies, though, often stay the same for years,

5
00:00:13.588 --> 00:00:17.778
and what fitted five years ago may cover too little today.

6
00:00:18.878 --> 00:00:22.569
Once a year, check that your beneficiaries are the people you want,

7
00:00:22.814 --> 00:00:26.203
that the sums insured are enough for today’s loans and family,

8
00:00:26.506 --> 00:00:31.381
that the amounts keep up with inflation, and when each policy renews.

9
00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:34.397
Look at your own policies together with what

10
00:00:34.397 --> 00:00:37.252
you have through work and through GESY.

11
00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:41.687
Often something is covered twice, and something else not at all.

12
00:00:42.787 --> 00:00:44.400
And before you change anything:

13
00:00:44.459 --> 00:00:46.560
do not cancel a policy before the new

14
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.812
one has been accepted and is in force.

15
00:00:49.114 --> 00:00:52.318
A new policy may exclude health conditions you already have,

16
00:00:52.505 --> 00:00:57.473
and cancelling a savings policy early often returns less than you paid in.

17
00:00:58.573 --> 00:01:03.495
Gather your policies, put premiums, renewal dates and beneficiaries on one page,

18
00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:06.246
and tell your family where it is kept.

19
00:01:07.346 --> 00:01:10.097
Run the free annual check on avrastro.com,

20
00:01:10.121 --> 00:01:12.233
and book a review with an advisor.
